     "text": {
      "en": "**PG focus**\n• Hayflick (1961): normal human fibroblasts divide about 50 times, a limit linked to telomere shortening.\n• Cross-contamination is a major problem: HeLa has overgrown many lines, so authenticate lines by STR profiling.\n• Test regularly for mycoplasma (PCR, Hoechst stain)."
