  {
   "id": "s10",
   "title": {
    "en": "Summary & Exam Revision"
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Key points and model answers likely to appear in university examinations."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "**Key exam points**"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "1"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Culture conditions: 37 °C, 5% CO₂, pH 7.2–7.4, humid, sterile; serum 5–10%."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "2"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Growth curve: lag, log, plateau, decline; subculture in log phase."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "3"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Normal cells have a finite life span (Hayflick limit ~50); continuous lines are transformed."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "4"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "HeLa, CHO, Vero, HEK-293, BHK-21: know origin and use."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "5"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Stem cell potency: totipotent > pluripotent > multipotent; iPSCs by Oct4, Sox2, Klf4, c-Myc."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "6"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Artificial skin: cultured keratinocytes on a collagen/fibroblast matrix."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "7"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Bioreactors: stirred tank, airlift, hollow fibre, packed bed; batch, fed-batch, perfusion."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "8"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Ethanol: pyruvate → acetaldehyde + CO₂ → ethanol; yeast; distillation."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "9"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "HGP: 1990–2003, 3.1 Gb, ~20 000 genes, ~1.5% coding; BAC vs shotgun."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "10"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Patent: novelty, inventive step, industrial application; 20 years in India; RCGM, GEAC, CPCSEA regulate."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "**Short-answer questions**"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Click a question to reveal the model answer."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.1List the requirements for animal cell culture.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Sterile vessel and aseptic technique; basal medium with serum or defined supplements; 37 °C; 5% CO₂ humidified atmosphere; pH 7.2–7.4 (bicarbonate buffer, phenol red indicator)."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.2Describe the growth curve of cultured cells.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Lag (adaptation), log (exponential growth), plateau (confluence, nutrient limitation) and decline (toxic waste, death). Subculture in log phase."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.3Differentiate primary culture and cell line.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Primary culture is taken directly from tissue; once subcultured it becomes a cell line, finite (40–60 doublings) or continuous (immortal, transformed)."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.4What are iPS cells?▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Pluripotent cells made by reprogramming somatic cells with Oct4, Sox2, Klf4 and c-Myc (Yamanaka 2006); patient-specific and avoid embryo destruction."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.5Describe a stirred-tank bioreactor.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "A vessel with impeller, sparger, probes for pH, dissolved oxygen and temperature, jacket, inlet and harvest ports; mixing and aeration are controlled for suspension cells."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.6Explain how ethanol is produced industrially.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Molasses or hydrolysed starch is fermented by _S. cerevisiae_ at 30–35 °C; wash with 7–10% ethanol is distilled to ~95% and dehydrated with molecular sieves."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.7Compare the two approaches to the Human Genome Project.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Public: hierarchical BAC mapping then shotgun of each clone. Celera: whole-genome shotgun and computer assembly. Both converged in 2001."
     }
    }
   ],
   "label": "📋 Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "s11",
   "title": {
    "en": "Key Terms & Glossary"
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Important terms in simple language."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Confluence"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Fraction of the surface covered by adherent cells."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Passage"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Transfer of cells into fresh vessels (subculture)."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Hayflick limit"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Finite number of divisions of normal cells."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Contact inhibition"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Stopping of growth when cells touch."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Pluripotent"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Able to form all three germ layers."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Perfusion"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Continuous supply of fresh medium with cell retention."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Sparger"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Device that bubbles gas into a bioreactor."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Contig"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Set of overlapping DNA clones or reads."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "BAC"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Bacterial artificial chromosome (100–200 kb)."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Prior art"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Existing knowledge that may defeat novelty of a patent."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "GEAC"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Genetic Engineering Appraisal Committee, India."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "3Rs"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Replace, Reduce, Refine in animal research."
     }
    }
   ],
   "label": "📖 Glossary"
  }
